    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0402" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4972b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-22T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Heid.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d320-f1"/> War Trade Board’s 189 June 25, 7
                        p.m.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d320-f2"/> Impression received here based on a
                    report from General Cecek<anchor n="1" xml:id="d320-f3"/> is that expenses <pb
                        facs="0403" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/> in connection with repatriation wounded
                    Czechoslovak soldiers are being borne by United States, and it is also reported
                    that this misapprehension has been spread throughout Siberia. For your
                    information, and kindly inform General Cecek and Dr. Girsa,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d320-f4"/> all expenses connected with repatriation of these
                    soldiers are being paid by Czechoslovak Legation here from funds loaned to
                    Czechoslovak Republic by United States Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d320-f1" n="98" xml:id="d320-f1-content">
                <p>August Heid, representative at Vladivostok of the War Trade Board.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d320-f2" n="99" xml:id="d320-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d320-f3" n="1" xml:id="d320-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Stanislav Ċeček, Czechoslovak Commander at Vladivostok.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d320-f4" n="2" xml:id="d320-f4-content">
                <p>Václav Girsa, Czechoslovak Commissioner in Siberia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
